            {
                "entry_id": "17516a67-a215-340c-b89a-5524ef9bb347",
                "word": "Hui",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e69711a4-019b-43c7-be7f-e6636d32f043",
                        "entry_id": "17516a67-a215-340c-b89a-5524ef9bb347",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "Huis"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c483fd8e-2099-3ae4-a9cf-356aa7977bfa",
                        "entry_id": "17516a67-a215-340c-b89a-5524ef9bb347",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Membre de l’ethnie chinoise de religion musulmane."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "note": "La plupart des Huis ne se distinguent des Hans que par la religion",
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "26d26bfa-8a8c-47c2-b202-32f0ea827cdd",
                                "sense_id": "c483fd8e-2099-3ae4-a9cf-356aa7977bfa",
                                "text": "De longue date, les Huis se sont dispersés à travers le territoire de la Chine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bac4bf8e-e87c-4b41-802b-d82f62b1f03b",
                                "sense_id": "c483fd8e-2099-3ae4-a9cf-356aa7977bfa",
                                "text": "Aujourd’hui, l’arrivée d’une nouvelle génération de responsables religieux, le renforcement des liens avec l’umma et le développement des autres religions prophétiques en Chine placent les Hui dans une nouvelle situation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c4b02822-ce02-4a7d-a077-f1515e0782c1",
                                "sense_id": "c483fd8e-2099-3ae4-a9cf-356aa7977bfa",
                                "text": "De nos jours, les musulmans chinois sont surtout des Hui (10 millions), des Ouïgours (8 millions), et des Kazakhs (1,3 million). La vaste majorité de la population chinoise, 70 %, est athée."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "341d49dc-5f44-4379-abe6-eb434ac2df48",
                        "source_entry_id": "17516a67-a215-340c-b89a-5524ef9bb347",
                        "source_sense_id": "c483fd8e-2099-3ae4-a9cf-356aa7977bfa",
                        "target_lang_word": "Hui",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Hui",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3ae80bcd-e2b9-3ed3-893b-04b1333cfee8",
                                        "entry_id": "ff6f3b7d-21af-3c66-aaa1-0d7f69b9b9df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An ethnic group of China, distinguished by their practice of Islam, who speak Mandarin (or Dungan in Kyrgyzstan, Kazakhstan, and Russia)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural",
                                            "plural-only"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1222ba9-9946-4166-ac04-8472c7d1f3c9",
                                                "sense_id": "3ae80bcd-e2b9-3ed3-893b-04b1333cfee8",
                                                "text": "In Hui restaurants in towns such as Wuchung and Chungning, restaurant workers wearing the white caps of the Hui nationality serve customers. Most government institutions, factories and schools in different parts of the autonomous region have set up dining rooms for the Huis, where their special foods are served."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14b1084b-3e63-4be8-998a-4cc7e10e3358",
                                                "sense_id": "3ae80bcd-e2b9-3ed3-893b-04b1333cfee8",
                                                "text": "This compact collection of households comprises nine teams that are almost 100 percent Hui, a rarity in central and northern Ningxia, where Hui are thinly distributed among the majority Han population. Yongning county is only 12.9 percent Hui, a relatively small minority in contrast to neighboring Lingwu county in the southeast, which is 47 percent Hui, and southern Jingyuan county, which is 97 percent Hui (the highest concentration of Hui in one county in China)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1123ec50-5dd2-4011-9ee5-d178ee0f2bd9",
                                                "sense_id": "3ae80bcd-e2b9-3ed3-893b-04b1333cfee8",
                                                "text": "Within Xi’an, Hui and Han alike eat roujiamo, the Chinese hamburger: meat tucked into flatbread that’s been crisped on the grill until it shows tiger skin on one side — shades of orange and black — and a chrysanthemum whorl on the other. The Han make it with long-braised pork, doused with a spoonful of its own broth, and the Hui with beef or lamb, stewed, then salted and dried."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
